From 4a1007332c38e31d5743cebbb19493b68fa6c480 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:47:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chamfer): a wall that leans in the frame is not a
 modelled chamfer

The #2887 check read the sections of a box stock under a tilted frame
as a loop bevelled on part of its length, and refused a legal no-pick
2D Chamfer. The top section of such a prism is its corner section moved
whole by one plan vector. `partly_bevelled` now reads that as no bevel
(`leans`), and the ride is the wall at the corner depth, as before
#2887. A loop bevelled on one side is no moved copy of its wall, so the
#2887 refusal holds.

Fixes #2936

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
